  "articleBody": "Hiring a contractor to turn an underused garage into an extra bedroom, home office, or guest suite is an exciting investment, but signing a contract before clarifying the scope can cause massive headaches. Converting parking into living space is rarely just cosmetic; it involves building regulations, moisture protection, and heating comfort.\n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide:\n- Are building regulations and local permits factored into the estimate?\n- How will the concrete slab be sealed against rising ground moisture before flooring goes down?\n- Who handles trade coordination for electrical circuits, heating, and plumbing rough-ins?\n- What are the wall and ceiling insulation specifications to keep the room warm through Colorado winters?\n- Is there an itemized breakdown showing labor, materials, and potential structural adjustments?\n\nA common mistake is skipping the damp-proofing assessment on the existing slab or assuming existing garage framing meets thermal standards. Having Abraham Becerra of HH Remodeling lead the project ensures hands-on carpentry, framing, drywall, and finish craftsmanship while trade partners are managed properly.\n\nReady to plan your garage conversion across the Denver area? Call HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss your layout, requirements, and project estimate.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
